  "case_id": "stair_riser_height__smiley",
  "rule": "Every stair must have risers between 100 mm and 180 mm high.\nRegulatory text (the authoritative clauses - use them to interpret the requirement and its applicability; you must still work out how to read or measure it from the IFC):\nADA and ABA Accessibility Guidelines (2004), 504.2 Treads and Risers: All steps on a flight of stairs shall have uniform riser heights and uniform tread depths. Risers shall be 4 inches (100 mm) high minimum and 7 inches (180 mm) high maximum. Treads shall be 11 inches (280 mm) deep minimum.\nBenchmark convention: judge every stair as a whole, from its steps as modelled in its geometry; recorded step properties may be missing, zero or inconsistent with the geometry. The limits apply in inches as written: 4 in = 101.6 mm and 7 in = 177.8 mm. A stair fails when its typical riser height (the height shared by its regular steps) is below 101.6 mm or above 177.8 mm. A first or last step that differs from the others is covered by a separate uniformity check, and tread depth by a separate tread check.\n\nLabel every stair.\nReport the GlobalId of every element (modelled as IfcStair) that does NOT satisfy this requirement.",
